{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351479-monster-lairs","id":1351479,"title":"Monster Lairs...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-28T07:59:39-08:00","id":1351479,"title":"Monster Lairs...","content":"So, I've been watching more D&amp;D-related videos on YouTube as of late, and Runesmith did a pretty good one about encounter design, and specifically <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8Lbw010KBt0\" target=\"_blank\">the fun that can be had in legendary creatures' lairs in 5e.</a> His video goes on about how having the scenery be significant to the battle makes the encounter more challenging and memorable than the PCs dogpiling an enemy and throwing numbers back and forth until it dies or they die.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is actually something I've always enjoyed the prospect of; if I feel the PCs are likely to fight somewhere, I try and have an appropriately dramatic locale in mind. In my Green Sun Princes game, for instance, I had a fight with a Solar akuma take place in a factory-cathedral that had been partially enveloped by a glacier. There were great mirrors set into the building to focus sunlight and make a spot near the center hot enough to forge orichalcum, but as half of them were blocked by encroaching ice, it was &quot;merely&quot; an environmental hazard equivalent to standing in a bonfire; a PC employing a Knockback effect could add damage to his attack by forcing the opposition into the pillar of sunlight (or vice-versa). Likewise, as the PCs traded blows with the Solar, big flashy attacks had the potential to damage the wall of ice and trigger mini-avalanches, adding further risk to the encounter.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Admittedly, this was still something of a failure, mostly because of the system of 2e. But one of my players <i>did</i> tell me that was one of the cooler fights.)<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat are some of the cooler places you've had a fight take place, and how did the location shape the fight in ways a featureless white void could never compare to?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:40:41-08:00","id":1351485,"title":"","content":"Well one fight in 2e I had take place starting at the top of the highest tower in a legendarily sized palace, then somebody triggered As In The Beginning and the second half of the battle took place as the palace crumbled and fell into the massive fissure that formed beneath it, with players leaping from a crumbling parapet to a half destroyed section of wall and eventually just bouncing around falling debris in free fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:59:34-08:00","id":1351489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the palace crumbled and fell into the massive fissure that formed beneath it, with players leaping from a crumbling parapet to a half destroyed section of wall </div> </div> </div>I did that once with a collapsing Manse.<br /> <br /> Last session of Lunars, the pack was on an airship when Blood Apes on Agatae materialised and leaped onto the balloon, swinging from ropes down to the ship itself.<br /> Two players stayed inside using the windows as cover, smashing windows down on Blood Apes's arms to send them falling into the void. Another clambered out and up to stand on top of the ship's hull, beneath the balloon, so he could swing his axe knocking the demons away. And one turned into an ape to challenge the apes, fighting their leader while both hung on with one arm to ropes hanging from the ship (with another PC throwing daggers at the demons' hand, until he eventually fell off).<br /> <br /> Maybe later I can do a fight between two airships, so they can jump back and forth or something. Definitely at some point I'll do them vs a Sky Serpent, as they're heading to the Elemental Pole of Air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}